<title>UK: BAA sees traffic growing at over five pct.</title>
<headline>BAA sees traffic growing at over five pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airports operator BAA Plc announced a 10.2 percent rise in underlying profits on Monday and said strong passenger growth was continuing with traffic expected to be up by over five percent in the current year.</p>
<p>The company said 98 million passengers passed through its seven British airports last year, up 4.6 percent on a year ago, which fuelled a 9.6 percent increase in turnover to 1.373 billion pounds from retailing, airport charges and property rentals.</p>
</text>
